 "text": "9/29/26, 10:19 AM\nThe maximum agreed offset and maximum notification offset are specified by way of the Customizing activity\nDefine Processing Variants for Disconnection Documents. You access this activity by way of the following path:\nSAPUtilities + CustomerService \u00bb Process Execution } Disconnection/Reconnection\n\nNotification Start Date and Due Date\n\nIf notification is required, the CRM agent must contact the customer within a specified time period:\n\ne The earliest date and time that the agent can contact the customer are defined as the notification start date and time.\n\ne The notification due date and time that appears on an agent's work list is defined as the notification due date and time \u2014\nnote however that it is still possible to contact the customer after this date, if required.\n\nThese dates and times are calculated using the planned disconnection date and time \u2014 more specifically, the system subtracts the\nstart date offset and due date offset from this date to determine the notification start and end dates.\n\nThe start date offset and due date offset are specified by way of the Customizing activity Define Processing Variants for\nDisconnection Documents. You access this activity by way of the following path: |\u00bbSAPUtilities s CustomerService Process\nExecution  Disconnection/Reconnection\n\nAn Agreed Date is Always Set in the Backend\n\nWhen notification is not required, an agreed date is not set from the standpoint of the user \u2014 however in the backend, the system\nautomatically sets the agreed date to equal the planned disconnection date.\n\nTherefore an agreed date is always set in the backend, whether or not customer notification is required.\n\nThe Agreed Date is the Actual Date That a Technician or the System Disconnects a Device\n\nDevices selected in the disconnection order are always disconnected on the agreed date , since it is set, either by customer\nnotification or by automatic mapping to the planned disconnection date.\n\nProcessing Disconnection Orders\n\nOnce an agreed date has been set, you can complete the disconnection order. Choose the Save button to save the order. If an\norder code and PM plant order number are provided, the system generates a service order, which can be processed by a service\n\ntechnician.\n\nGenerating Disconnection Orders Without a Dialog\n\nDisconnection orders can also be generated without a dialog. However, you do not have any control over the number of objects to\nbe disconnected or over the other parameters in this case.\n\nMonitoring Disconnection Activities\n\nYou can monitor the status of disconnection orders and access all corresponding screens related to these orders (for example,\nobject information screen, work order information screen) . For more information, see Monitoring Disconnection and Reconnection\nActivities .\n\nChanging Disconnection Dates\n\ne Customer requests \u2014 changing the agreed date\n",
